  "movement_and_persuasion_dynamics": {
    "Colleagues 1, 2, 3, 5": "They are completely unified around the pitch-class transposition argument (Fm -> Am is +4 semitones, G#/Ab -> B#/C, Pitch Class 0 is listed as C). Their strongest weapon remains the melodic voice-leading constraint: Kern's melody holds the exact same auditory pitch across the seam ('are' -> 'Some'), meaning G# would require an unwritten major 3rd leap (G# -> C).",
    "Colleagues 4, 6, 7": "Our offensive on the semantic/definitional contradiction of 'enharmonic respelling' (C to C is a diatonic common tone, not an enharmonic respelling; pitch-class integers are notation-agnostic so enharmonics don't exist in modular arithmetic; B# is absent; G# is the source note) is our strongest theoretical lever. It puts the majority on the defensive regarding engraving and test question grammar."
